WEBVTT

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:22.040
Toki-kun...

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:23.460
Hm?

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:24.660
The hot water.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:27.370
Oh, shoot!

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:30.130
What's going on? You seem distracted.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.730
Nothing, it's just that...

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:34.020
Just what?

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:35.850
Well...

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:41.520
It's about Himeno.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:46.390
So around dawn this morning, 
I was up to use the toilet.

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:52.810
Himeno, what are you doing?

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:55.560
Sorry, but can you not talk to me right now?

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:56.400
Huh?

00:00:58.430 --> 00:00:59.210
Yes.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:10.230
She seemed totally normal 
when she left this morning.

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:15.370
I'm pretty sure this is all because 
of all the things I said.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:20.340
I wonder what it is...

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:57.440
<b>Freedom - Future - Sparkle</b>

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:59.530
<i>It came to me when I looked at 
my mom's mugs this morning!</i>

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.890
<i>Yeah! I can do this!</i>

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.480
Wait, wait, Hime-chan!

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:10.420
Why are you race walking?

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:13.420
Because we can't run in the halls.

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:16.090
Which is why, from here...

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:21.720
I'll run like hell!

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:25.300
Wait... Wait, Hime-chan!

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:28.680
What's gotten into you, Hime-chan?!

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:31.520
You're too slow, Kukuri-chan.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:34.350
You're too fast!

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:46.540
Pernod Baron, sortie!

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:48.130
Heh.

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:24.200
Toyokawa-san, that's good!

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:27.570
What is?

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:30.730
You're putting zero excess 
force into that. It's perfect!

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:32.740
Oh, really?

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:35.210
I'm jealous. You got praised.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:48.740
<i>It's strange.</i>

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:56.420
<i>When I first came here, I didn't 
know the first thing about pottery.</i>

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:59.450
<i>Back then,</i>

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:06.260
<i>I was magically able to do well because 
Touko-senpai was holding my hands.</i>

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:11.970
I think that will do.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:15.300
Now try to push it out with your right hand.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.930
Just like that! That's great!

00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:22.420
For your first time, that was quite good.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:29.970
<i>That made me get cocky and 
I ended up ruining it.</i>

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:35.480
Hello!

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:36.900
Huh?

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:39.440
That's already out?

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:42.980
This is the third issue by now.

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:44.560
I see.

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:45.980
Where's the boss?

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:48.890
Do you mind waiting a bit?

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:52.240
He's in a dungeon right now and 
can't come out for a while.

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:56.670
Himena...

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:01.630
I know I said I'd take care 
of Himeno, and still...

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:03.010
I'm sorry.

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:07.520
Instead I pressured her and 
now she doesn't know what to do.

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:12.770
I need to do better than this.

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:26.210
<i>It's just like I imagined.</i>

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:28.700
<i>This is good!</i>

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:35.510
<i>Just a little bit more.</i>

00:06:41.350 --> 00:06:44.040
<i>Isn't this just perfect?</i>

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:49.960
Toyokawa-san is making such 
a nice face right now.

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:52.220
It's the "runru~" face.

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:58.780
I'm saving this one forever.

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:01.780
Yeah.

00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:03.790
That reminds me!

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:06.980
What is it?

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:09.360
I just thought of a different pattern.

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:20.100
What's this?

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:22.210
Having some nostalgia?

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:26.330
She's got a good head on her shoulders, 
but she did want to be coddled.

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:33.690
Whenever she went out, she'd come 
and ask, "Are these clothes okay?"

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:36.520
Is that so?

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:41.750
Before the last contest, she came 
to discuss it with me, too.

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:46.050
But this time she didn't say anything.

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:51.050
Probably because I'm the 
one who suggested it.

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:53.430
Well, she is a high school girl.

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:56.280
Not asking your parents for 
advice is normal at this age.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:58.870
Sixteen is practically an adult.

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:01.470
Is it?

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:12.520
I guess that might be true...

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:23.580
Okay, so what's going on, Hime-chan?

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:25.910
You're really pumping these out fast!

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:31.770
I don't think she can hear you.

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:36.160
Her concentrating face is also so good.

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:39.400
I wonder what she'll make next.

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:41.380
I don't think she can stop.

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:43.280
That's amazing.

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:44.650
I need to take more pictures.

00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:45.410
Bam!

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:49.940
What, what? Were you all watching me?

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:53.440
We were! And that looked really good!

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:54.850
I don't know...

00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:56.930
There was something about 
it that was slightly off.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:01.150
Toyokawa-san, you've really 
gotten more confident.

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:03.080
What do you mean?

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:06.930
Being able to throw away something 
you'd made is a sign of that.

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:09.160
I know what you mean!

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:10.760
When you first start,

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:12.400
it always feels so bad 
throwing anything away.

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:14.900
You figure it's taken so 
much to get to that point.

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:20.950
<i>Oh. I never felt that before...</i>

00:09:21.630 --> 00:09:23.670
<i>So that's what confidence is.</i>

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:28.760
<i>When I made the pillow,
I borrowed my mother's colors,</i>

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:30.890
<i>but not this time!</i>

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:35.570
<i>I'm... not lost!</i>

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:38.340
<i>It's fun.</i>

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:42.600
<i>My body's on fire,</i>

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:47.360
<i>and really, I'm having fun!</i>

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:49.680
<i>I'm having so much fun!</i>

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:03.830
Good evening!

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:07.050
Oh, welcome back.

00:10:07.570 --> 00:10:10.070
You're wiping the windows this late?

00:10:10.070 --> 00:10:13.140
It's easier to see the dirt in the evening.

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:17.590
Um, where's Himeno?

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:21.390
In her current state, I don't think 
she'll be coming home anytime soon.

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:22.330
What?

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:27.740
Even I thought it would be better to leave 
her alone, so I came home by myself.

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:29.060
See you later!

00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:38.280
Himeno...

00:10:50.070 --> 00:10:52.730
Hey! You should probably go home.

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:18.890
There's something wrong with me...

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:20.690
What do you mean?

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:26.800
All this time, I was cheering Himeno on, 
wishing the best for her.

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:29.630
But today, for the first time, 
I felt something else.

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:31.420
Which was?

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:33.530
That I was jealous.

00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:37.510
That I'm want to make 
something even better.

00:11:39.060 --> 00:11:42.170
I don't want to be like that.

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:45.680
It's all right, Mika-chan.

00:11:47.570 --> 00:11:51.510
It means that now you acknowledge 
Toyokawa-san even more than before.

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:59.320
You'll be able to become good rivals, 
and even better friends now.

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:05.770
I see.

00:12:08.420 --> 00:12:10.930
We will!

00:12:12.070 --> 00:12:14.080
We will be like that!

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:17.350
I see it!

00:12:17.350 --> 00:12:19.360
That's good.

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:22.260
Sensei?

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:24.190
How long have you been here?

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:27.300
For five minutes or so.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:30.740
I'm sorry! I didn't notice at all!

00:12:30.740 --> 00:12:32.230
It's not a problem.

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:34.300
So, what about the thing you saw?

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:35.190
What now?

00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:42.500
Can I just stay for a little bit longer?

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:45.410
Sure. I'll wait.

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:47.130
Thank you so much!

00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:27.780
The bob-haired girl finally did it!

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:35.350
<b>Mini-Mini Pottery Club</b>

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:30.220
Everyone was waiting for you.

00:14:30.490 --> 00:14:33.280
And now you're...

00:14:33.780 --> 00:14:36.850
Next up, "I'm Making a Mug!"

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:37.430
<b>Next Time:</b>

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:40.010
<b>I'm Making a Mug!</b>

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:39.590
No matter how far apart we are, 
we'll still be connected.
